### Listings API — Endpoints/ListingsApiEndpoints.cs (P4.3 caching + rate
### limiting, P4.4 file storage). Reads are public; the photo upload is
### gated to the ListingsWriter policy (any signed-in user).
###
### Rate limit: 5 requests / 10s per client, fixed window ("Api" policy) —
### hammering this file will 429. Reads are also cached 30s server-side
### ("Listings" output-cache policy) — a repeat GET within that window
### returns the cached response even after data changes; see docs/caching.md.

@baseUrl = https://localhost:7105

### Get all listings
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/listings

### Get one listing
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/listings/1

### Get a listing that doesn't exist — expect 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/listings/999999

### Upload a photo — needs a real session, not runnable as-is.
### This endpoint is [Authorize(Policy = "ListingsWriter")] (cookie auth) and
### form-bound, so ASP.NET Core's automatic antiforgery validation applies
### (dotnet-aspnetcore:minimal-api-file-upload) — a raw request needs both
### the auth cookie AND a matching __RequestVerificationToken form field, not
### just a bearer token. Easiest way to get both: log in through the app in a
### browser, open dev tools' Network tab, find the antiforgery cookie value
### and copy a __RequestVerificationToken from any rendered <form> on the
### site, then substitute them below. Swap {{authCookie}} / {{csrfToken}} for
### real values, and update the boundary/id to match.
# @no-redirect
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/listings/1/photo
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary
Cookie: .AspNetCore.Identity.Application={{authCookie}}

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="__RequestVerificationToken"

{{csrfToken}}
------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="photo.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./sample-photo.jpg
------boundary--
